<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-CURRIE CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-CURRIE CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<text>
<p>EAST LONDON, June 22 (Reuter)S - Results of the Currie Cup</p>
<p>rugby union matches played over the weekend:</p>
<p>Natal beat South Western Districts 26-22 (halftime 17-9).</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Natal - Tries: Wayne Fyvie, Joos Joubert. Conversions: Gavin</p>
<p>Lawless (2). Penalties: Lawless (3). Drop goal: Hans Scriba.</p>
<p>South Western Districts - Try: Pine Pienaar. Conversion:</p>
<p>Braam van Straaten. Penalties: van Straaten (5).</p>
<p>Border beat Mpumalanga 41-23 (halftime 22-20).</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Border - Tries: Anton Botha, Lyle Blakeway, Khaya Malotana,</p>
<p>David Maidza. Coversions: Greg Miller (3). Penalties: Miller</p>
<p>(5).</p>
<p>Mpumalanga - Tries: Henry Kemp, Francois Rossouw (2).</p>
<p>Coversion: Eben von Gericke. Penalties: Von Gericke (2).</p>
<p>Standings (tabulated under - played, won, drawn, lost,</p>
<p>points for, points against, bonus points, total points) :</p>
<p>    Griqualand West	   2   2   0   0   106    35   2   10</p>
<p>    Natal			 2   2   0   0    60    44   0    8</p>
<p>    Boland			2   1   0   1    62    58   2    6</p>
<p>    Gauteng Falcons	   2   1   0   1    71   106   2    6</p>
<p>    North West		  2   1   0   1    97    54   1    5</p>
<p>    Free State		  1   1   0   0    56    19   1    5</p>
<p>    Western Province	  2   1   0   1    97    66   1    5</p>
<p>    Gauteng Lions	     1   1   0   0    35    33   1    5</p>
<p>    South Western Districts 3   1   0   2    69    87   1    5</p>
<p>    Northern Free State     2   1   0   1    49    81   1    5</p>
<p>    Border			2   1   0   1    56    89   1    5</p>
<p>    Northern Transvaal	1   0   0   1    18    30   0    0</p>
<p>    Mpumalanga		  2   0   0   2    42    97   0    0</p>
<p>    Eastern Province	  2   0   0   2    41    60   0    0</p>
